// CallSite args are a sequential SCOPE CHAIN and must evaluate in
// SOURCE ORDER (fixed 2026-08-06): the args map was an AHashMap
// iterated by update(), so whether the #n subtree's `let x` bind ran
// before the sibling reader `array::iter(x)` was a per-process ahash
// coin flip — ~half of processes silently starved (the bind's
// same-cycle delivery landed after the reader's update; never
// redelivered), the rest emitted [1,2,3]. Args are now an
// insertion-ordered IndexMap (insertion = source order).
// TRIPWIRE NOTE: on a broken binary this pin only trips when the two
// contexts' coins land differently (~40%) — a flap here is ALWAYS
// this class, rerun to confirm rather than dismissing as noise.
array::group(skip(#n: let x = [i64:1, i64:2, i64:3], array::iter(x)), |n, _| n == i64:3)
